👤 IAM User – Description

IAM = Identity and Access Management

An IAM User is an identity created within an AWS account for a person or application.

IAM Users are used to access AWS services securely.

The Root User or AWS administrator can create IAM Users.

Each IAM User can be given specific permissions.

Access can be controlled based on the user's role and responsibilities.

IAM Users can access selected AWS services such as:
Amazon S3
Amazon EC2
Amazon RDS

=======

Simple Definition

An IAM User is a user created in an AWS account with specific permissions to access and manage AWS resources.

Easy Difference

| Root User                  | IAM User                             |
| -------------------------- | ------------------------------------ |
| Main AWS account owner     | User created inside the AWS account  |
| Full access                | Access based on assigned permissions |
| Controls the whole account | Accesses only allowed resources      |

===

An IAM User provides controlled access to AWS resources, and 
its permissions should be assigned through IAM policies based on the user's job responsibilities to follow the principle of least privilege.

